# s1-page-virtual-client desktop wiring

## 1. Route (apps/desktop/src/shared/core-lanes/desktop-operation-route.ts, hot-adjacent, not owned by this task)
In the "local pages served by the core page server" block, after the `localPageVirtualIn` line add:

    localPageAssetType: positional('projectFs/localPage/assetType', ['root', 'file', 'dataRoot']),

and in the reply table after `localPageVirtualIn: (reply) => record(reply).url,` add:

    // The core answers {type}; '' when the file is not served.
    localPageAssetType: (reply) => String(record(reply).type ?? ''),

Add 'localPageAssetType' beside 'localPageVirtualIn' in the name list of protocol/desktop-operation-route.test.mjs (line ~368).
Update the comment on the localPageVirtualIn row: CoreLocalPages.virtual (renamed from virtualUrl) maps the Record to it.

## 2. index.ts (DESKTOP-WIRE-G4)
The renderer CSP frame-src keeps ONE loopback page origin: the core's (coreLocalPages().origin()). Drop the Electron page server's
origin (localPageOrigin() of local-page-server.ts) from frame-src. After that nothing calls local-page-server.ts except its own
tests: its deletion task removes local-page-server.ts, local-page-server.test.mjs, and moves visualize/inline-page.test.mjs and
local-page-permissions.test.mjs virtual cases (they still import localVirtualPageUrl) to the core replays.

## 3. Needs the core method projectFs/localPage/assetType (see pending-rows and core pending-wire of this task)

## 4. visualize/service.slow.test.mjs (not owned here)
Its fake core invoke (setCoreLocalPages(createCoreLocalPages(...)), line ~46) throws on any call but localPageUrlIn. Version snapshots now call
localPageAssetType and inline pages / exports call localPageVirtualIn. Answer localPageAssetType with the Electron pageAssetType(root, file, dataRoot)
until local-page-server.ts is deleted, and then with a table by extension; answer localPageVirtualIn with a fixed loopback url.

## 5. visualize/versions.test.mjs (not owned here; fails until this is applied)
collectSnapshot now asks coreLocalPages().assetType for each page asset, and versions.test.mjs sets no core page client:
"a version is kept only when the files changed, with the page assets it uses" and "panes from different folders keep their
files apart and restore back where they came from" fail with "The local page server is not connected.". At the top of the
file add (imports beside the others):

    import { createCoreLocalPages, setCoreLocalPages } from '../core-local-pages.ts';
    import { pageAssetType } from '../local-page-server.ts';
    // The core page server's asset policy stands behind coreLocalPages(); here the shared policy answers the same call.
    setCoreLocalPages(
      createCoreLocalPages(async (name, [root, file, dataRoot]) => {
        if (name === 'localPageAssetType') return pageAssetType(root, file, dataRoot);
        throw new Error(`unexpected core call ${name}`);
      })
    );

The deletion task of local-page-server.ts replaces pageAssetType there as in item 4 (the test needs '.cache/x.js' refused and
css/js served).

## 6. Client input corpus
After item 1, regenerate native/core/crates/mixdog-app-protocol/src/boundary/validate/fixtures/clients-accepted.json with
scripts/collect-client-inputs.mjs so projectFs/localPage/assetType has its desktop row (ownerDirection 3).
